<!-- DEFINITION -->
<section class="chapter def" id="definition" data-chapter="Definition" data-part="2">
  <div class="def-pin" id="def-pin">
    <div class="def-word" aria-label="NoSQL means not only SQL">
      <span class="w w1">NoSQL</span>
      <span class="w w2"><s>No SQL</s></span>
      <span class="w w3"><span class="sm">Not only</span>SQL</span>
    </div>
    <p class="def-cap" id="def-cap">The name first read as a refusal. It grew into an invitation.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="def-read">
    <p class="eyebrow">Definition</p>
    <p class="def-para" id="def-para">A <span class="hl">NoSQL database</span> stores and retrieves data with <span class="hl2">less constrained consistency models</span> than a traditional relational database. It is an <span class="hl">umbrella term</span> for every data store that does not follow RDBMS principles: a class of products, and a collection of related ideas about storing and handling data, usually at large scale.</p>
    <blockquote class="def-quote">
      <p>“Next generation databases mostly addressing some of the points: being <b>non-relational</b>, <b>distributed</b>, <b>open-source</b> and <b>horizontally scalable</b>. The original intention has been modern web-scale databases. Often more characteristics apply such as: schema-free, easy replication support, simple API, eventually consistent / BASE (not ACID), a huge amount of data and more.”</p>
      <cite>nosql-database.org</cite>
    </blockquote>
    <div class="def-facts">
      <div><span class="big">3</span><p>Readings of the name: <b>No relational</b>, <b>No RDBMS</b>, and the one that stuck, <b>Not only SQL</b>.</p></div>
      <div><span class="big">4</span><p>Main data models: key-value, document, column-family and graph.</p></div>
      <div><span class="big">SQL-ish</span><p>Many allow SQL-like languages: Cassandra has CQL, Couchbase has SQL++. “No SQL” was never the point.</p></div>
      <div><span class="big">Not new</span><p>Non-relational DBMSs existed before. NoSQL is a new incarnation, driven by internet-scale apps and distributed, parallel computing.</p></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
    <!-- 04 TIMELINE -->
    <section class="chapter tl" id="origins" data-scene="strand" data-chapter="Origins" data-part="2">
      <div class="tl-sticky">
